caption: Core Shido
domain-rule: core-shido

Upon entering the Kung Fu Domain, the practitioner must declare one Core Shido. The Core Shido must be a Code of Honor, Sense of Duty, or Intolerance that qualifies as a Voluntary Mental Disadvantage under the Tier 1 rules.

The Core Shido defines the scope of the practitioner's Kung Fu Higher Purpose under Martial Class Details. It is fixed when the Domain is entered. If Kung Fu is learned institutionally, the school fixes its Core Shido and the practitioner must accept that Shido as part of entering the school. If Class access permits the practitioner to enter Kung Fu without an institutional school, the practitioner chooses a legal Core Shido at that time.

For Gaoshou, the Kung Fu Core Shido is also the Style's first Style Shido, associated with Duan Wei 1. It is not an additional Shido beyond the Style's normal five.
